To find a dataset that maps honorifics to names in different formats and filter the results based on a specific location using C# code, you can use a search engine or a dataset repository website such as Kaggle or UCI Machine Learning Repository. Once you have found a suitable dataset, you can download it and load it into your C# application.
To extract the honorific for a given name while accounting for possible variations in the name spelling and order, you can use regular expressions to match the name against the names in the dataset. You can also use string manipulation functions to split the name into its constituent parts and compare them to the names in the dataset.
Here is an example of C# code that extracts the honorific for the name "John Smith" from a CSV dataset that contains the following entries:
```
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;
class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string csvFilePath = "path/to/dataset.csv";
        string nameToFind = "John Smith";
        string[] lines = File.ReadAllLines(csvFilePath);
        string[] headers = lines[0].Split(',');
        int nameIndex = Array.IndexOf(headers, "Full Name");
        int honorificIndex = Array.IndexOf(headers, "Honorific");
        string honorific = null;
        foreach (string line in lines.Skip(1))
        {
            string[] fields = line.Split(',');
            string fullName = fields[nameIndex];
            string[] nameParts = fullName.Split(' ');
            if (nameParts.Length < 2)
            {
                continue;
            }
            string firstName = nameParts[0];
            string lastName = nameParts[nameParts.Length - 1];
            if (firstName.Equals(nameToFind.Split(' ')[0], StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                && lastName.Equals(nameToFind.Split(' ')[1], StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            {
                honorific = fields[honorificIndex];
                break;
            }
        }
        Console.WriteLine($"Honorific for {nameToFind}: {honorific}");
    }
}
```
This code reads in the CSV file and searches for the honorific associated with the name "John Smith". It splits each line of the CSV file into fields using the comma separator. Then, it splits the full name field into first and last name parts. It compares the first and last name parts with the name to find and if they match, it assigns the corresponding honorific to the `honorific` variable. Finally, it prints out the honorific for the given name.

