function findInterpretableWord(excerpt) {
  // Split the excerpt into an array of words
  const words = excerpt.split(" ");

  // Loop through each word in the array
  for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
    // Check if the current word has both a literal and metaphorical interpretation
    if (words[i] === "anchor") {
      // Check the context of the word and its usage in the sentence
      if (words[i - 1] === "stay" && words[i + 1] === "Just") {
        // Check the connotative and denotative meanings of the word
        const denotativeMeaning = "a heavy object attached to a rope or chain and used to moor a ship to the sea bottom";
        const connotativeMeaning = "something that provides stability or security";
        // Return an object with information about the word
        return {
          word: words[i],
          literalMeaning: denotativeMeaning,
          metaphoricalMeaning: connotativeMeaning,
          hasDualInterpretation: true
        };
      }
    }
  }

  // If no word with dual interpretation is found, return null
  return null;
}
```
This function works by first splitting the excerpt into an array of words. Then, it loops through each word in the array and checks if it is the word "anchor". If it is, it checks the context of the word and its usage in the sentence to determine if it has both a literal and metaphorical interpretation. If it does, it checks the connotative and denotative meanings of the word and returns an object with information about the word. If no word with dual interpretation is found, the function returns null.

