5. Repeat steps 3-4 for each planet in the solar system that the spacecraft will encounter on its journey.
6. To factor in the gravitational pulls of each planet and optimize the journey, you can use a technique called gravitational assist maneuvers. This involves using the gravitational pull of a planet to alter the spacecraft's trajectory and increase its velocity, allowing it to travel further with less fuel. To implement this in your JavaScript code, you can calculate the trajectory of the spacecraft using the gravitational pull of each planet it encounters, and adjust the spacecraft's velocity accordingly.
