Once you've configured the endpoint, you can test your voice commands using the Alexa Skills Kit (ASK) Developer Console or an Alexa-enabled device. You can use the ASK Developer Console to simulate voice requests and see how Alexa responds.
6. Integrate third-party APIs and services to extend the functionality of your voice command system.
To add more advanced functionality to your voice command system, you can integrate third-party APIs and services. For example, you can use the Spotify API to play music or the Google Calendar API to set reminders.
Here's an example Lambda function that uses the Spotify API to play a song:
```python
import spotipy
from spotipy.oauth2 import SpotifyOAuth
sp = spotipy.Spotify(auth_manager=SpotifyOAuth(client_id='YOUR_CLIENT_ID',
                                               client_secret='YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET',
                                               redirect_uri='YOUR_REDIRECT_URI',
                                               scope='user-read-playback-state,user-modify-playback-state'))
def lambda_handler(event, context):
    track = event['request']['intent']['slots']['Track']['value']
    results = sp.search(q=track, type='track')
    if results['tracks']['items']:
        track_uri = results['tracks']['items'][0]['uri']
        sp.start_playback(uris=[track_uri])
        return {
            'version': '1.0',
            'response': {
                'outputSpeech': {
                    'type': 'PlainText',
                    'text': 'Playing ' + track
                },
                'shouldEndSession': True
            }
        }
    else:
        return {
            'version': '1.0',
            'response': {
                'outputSpeech': {
                    'type': 'PlainText',
                    'text': 'Sorry, I could not find ' + track
                },
                'shouldEndSession': True
            }
        }
```
This Lambda function uses the Spotipy library to search for a song and play it on the user's Spotify account. It expects the voice command to include a slot called "Track" that specifies the name of the song to play.
